{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Fallen and St. Anger fit my interest in heavy guitars, with melodic vocals in one case and aggressive intensity in the other.",
    "American Idiot connects with the energetic punk rock side of my interest in Chuck, while Led Zeppelin IV offers the powerful riffs I also enjoy."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Beatles collections and Eagles compilation share a broad rock connection with my listening, but they do not offer the sustained heaviness or intensity I want right now.",
    "Adele's vocal pop does not match my current guitar-driven interests, and Partners gives me too little information to expect a relevant match."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seem to lean too heavily on widely known albums; familiarity alone does not make me interested in listening now.",
    "My interest in rock seems to have been stretched to include music with quite different energy and guitar sounds."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated interactions with Colony, Reroute to Remain, Soundtrack to Your Escape, and Figure Number Five suggest that heavy riffs paired with melody matter to me.",
    "My latest choices, Ten Thousand Fists and 10.000 Days, reinforce an interest in forceful, guitar-driven music that deserves more attention."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in energetic rock, but drifted toward famous albums beyond my current preference for heavy, riff-driven music."
}"}
